comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-03T17:26:41.815Z","harness:pi","CodeQL alert #1 (js/polynomial-redos, high) at index.ts:245 — the regex /\\/+$\\/u in readConfig's orgUrl.replace() backtracks O(n²) on adversarial input (50k slashes + 'a' + 50k slashes). Measured timing BEFORE fix (old regex): 4641ms for a 100001-char witness. AFTER fix (backward charCodeAt scan): 1.2ms. Regression test asserts <50ms hard bound. Witness: '/'.repeat(50000) + 'a' + '/'.repeat(50000). Stash proof: test FAILS without fix (4641ms > 50ms), PASSES with fix (1.2ms < 50ms)."
tests[1]{command,path,scope,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref},note}:
  node --test test/ado.test.ts,test/ado.test.ts,project,"harness:pi","2026-09-03T17:27:08.400Z",local_mutation,main,readConfig strips a ReDoS-adversarial org URL within a hard time bound
docs[1]{path,scope,note}:
  "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/security/code-scanning/1",project,js/polynomial-redos
close_reason: "Fixed: replaced the polynomial-redos regex /\\/+$\\/u in readConfig with a backward charCodeAt scan (O(n), no backtracking). Regression test proves the fix: adversarial input of 100001 chars (50k slashes + 'a' + 50k slashes) completes in 1.2ms with the fix vs 4641ms without it. Stash proof verified: test fails without fix, passes with fix."
